//@version=6
// ╔══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════╗
// ║ TI-A — adaptive, abstention-first trading indicator (TradingView port)    ║
// ╚══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════╝
//
// TWO OPERATING MODES (Settings ▸ Inputs ▸ Mode):
//
//   A) "Frozen Research Model — NOT market-validated"
//      Evaluates the model exported by the Python reference, through the
//      original gate: a 90% lower credible bound on expectancy, net of
//      modelled costs. That gate is deliberately NOT relaxed here. On most
//      charts it will show NO TRADE forever, and the card prints the exact
//      arithmetic (edge bound, cost, shortfall) so you can see why. That is
//      the honest output of a model whose edge is unproven — not a bug.
//
//   B) "Practical Observation Mode"                       <- default
//      The SAME feature stack and the SAME engines, gated by a
//      reliability-weighted score with adjustable strictness, so a chart
//      produces enough signals to observe and paper-test. It carries no
//      claim of validation whatsoever and is backed by no backtest.
//
//      READ THIS ONE SENTENCE BEFORE USING MODE B. It was measured firing
//      ~21 times per 4000 bars on a SYNTHETIC MARTINGALE -- a market with no
//      edge in it at all, by construction. Mode A fired 0-1 times on the same
//      data. Mode B is therefore a tool for SEEING what the engines react to,
//      not evidence that what they react to is tradeable. If you want the
//      gate that abstains on noise, that is Mode A, and its answer is
//      usually "no trade".
//
// WHAT THIS IS NOT: it is not an RSI/MACD/moving-average crossover in a
// costume. The evidence is a 4-state regime posterior (products of Beta
// densities over rank features, zero parameters fitted to returns), a Kalman
// local-linear-trend t-statistic, a liquidity-adjusted displacement ratio, a
// volume-absorption measure, a confirmed-pivot sweep-and-fail detector, a
// Lo-MacKinlay variance ratio, and permutation entropy - pooled with
// correlation-aware weights rather than added up.
//
// NON-REPAINTING, STRUCTURALLY:
//   * every signal is emitted only on a CONFIRMED (closed) bar;
//   * no request.security() anywhere - the higher timeframe is aggregated
//     inside the script from closed chart bars, so it is valid on 1m, 1h, 1D
//     and 1W charts alike and cannot look ahead;
//   * pivots are invisible until confirmed; a sweep is knowable only after it
//     has failed; when a bar's range spans both barriers the STOP is taken,
//     and a gap through the stop is treated as filled at the open.
//
// WARM-UP: ~300 bars. The card counts it down.
// NOT INVESTMENT ADVICE. No profitability is claimed anywhere in this script.
// See docs/20-FINAL-REVIEW.md for what is and is not established.

indicator("TI-A", shorttitle="TI-A", overlay=true, max_bars_back=500,
     max_labels_count=500, max_lines_count=500, max_boxes_count=500)

// ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
// INPUTS
// ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
string MODE_A = "A: Frozen Research Model (not market-validated)"
string MODE_B = "B: Practical Observation Mode"

string modeIn      = input.string(MODE_B, "Operating mode", options=[MODE_B, MODE_A], group="Mode",
     tooltip="A evaluates the exported research model through its original, unrelaxed gate and will almost never signal. B is a chart-practical gate built from the same features.")
int    strictIn    = input.int(3, "Signal strictness (Mode B)", minval=1, maxval=5, group="Mode",
     tooltip="1 = loose (most signals) ... 5 = strict (fewest). Mode B only; Mode A ignores it.")

bool   allowLong   = input.bool(true,  "Allow long entries",  group="Direction")
bool   allowShort  = input.bool(true,  "Allow short entries", group="Direction")

bool   useHtfConf  = input.bool(true,  "Require higher-timeframe agreement", group="Filters")
bool   useSession  = input.bool(false, "Limit entries to a session (intraday charts only)", group="Filters")
string sessIn      = input.session("0930-1600", "Session", group="Filters")
int    cooldownIn  = input.int(10, "Cooldown bars after an exit", minval=0, maxval=200, group="Filters")
int    maxPer100In = input.int(6,  "Max entries per 100 bars", minval=1, maxval=50, group="Filters",
     tooltip="Mode A always uses the frozen model's own rate limit instead of this value.")

string STOP_ATR   = "ATR multiple"
string STOP_VOL   = "Forecast volatility (model default)"
string stopModeIn = input.string(STOP_VOL, "Stop / target basis", options=[STOP_VOL, STOP_ATR], group="Risk")
float  atrMultIn  = input.float(2.0, "ATR multiple for the stop", minval=0.25, maxval=10.0, step=0.25, group="Risk")
float  rrIn       = input.float(1.625, "Target : stop ratio (ATR mode)", minval=0.25, maxval=10.0, step=0.125, group="Risk",
     tooltip="1.625 reproduces the frozen model's 2.6 sigma target against its 1.6 sigma stop.")

string CARD_OFF  = "Off"
string CARD_MINI = "Compact"
string CARD_FULL = "Detailed"
string cardModeIn = input.string(CARD_MINI, "Status panel", options=[CARD_MINI, CARD_FULL, CARD_OFF], group="Display",
     tooltip="Compact shows what you act on. Detailed adds every engine reading underneath.")
string cardPosIn  = input.string("Top right", "Panel position", options=["Top right", "Middle right", "Bottom right", "Top left", "Bottom left"], group="Display")
string cardSizeIn = input.string("Small", "Panel text size", options=["Tiny", "Small", "Normal"], group="Display")

bool   showTrades = input.bool(true,  "Draw trades on the chart", group="Display",
     tooltip="Risk and reward zones drawn from the entry bar to the exit bar. These are anchored to bars, so they zoom and pan with the candles.")
bool   showMarks  = input.bool(true,  "Entry / exit markers", group="Display")
bool   showResult = input.bool(true,  "Label each exit with its result in R", group="Display",
     tooltip="R is the trade's move divided by its own initial risk. +1R means it made exactly what it risked.")
bool   showRegime = input.bool(true,  "Tint background by regime", group="Display")

color  upCol   = input.color(#26a69a, "Long colour",  group="Display", inline="col")
color  dnCol   = input.color(#ef5350, "Short colour", group="Display", inline="col")

bool isModeA = modeIn == MODE_A

// ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
// ==== BEGIN SHARED CORE ====
// Everything between these markers is BYTE-IDENTICAL in TIA.pine and
// TIA_strategy.pine, and python/tests/test_pine_port.py fails the build if it
// ever stops being. The two scripts therefore cannot drift apart: whatever the
// indicator paints, the strategy trades. Only the code after the END marker
// differs -- the indicator draws, the strategy places orders.
//
// The core requires exactly two names from the host file: `isModeA` and
// `strictIn`. It defines everything else it uses.
// ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

